<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Cultures</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Cultures of South &amp; Southeast Asia</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on 8 cultures of South &amp; Southeast Asia, from the Mehrgarh culture to the Sangam-age Tamilakam. Read their profiles, then answer.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=South%20%26%20Southeast%20Asia">Open the cultures &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the cultures from 1 (the earliest to begin) to 7 (the latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Vedic civilisation</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Indus Valley Civilisation</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>South Indian megalithic culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Painted Grey Ware culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Ban Chiang culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Dong Son culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Mehrgarh culture</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right homeland next to each culture. Their profiles will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Mehrgarh culture</li><li>Indus Valley Civilisation</li><li>Ban Chiang culture</li><li>Vedic civilisation</li><li>South Indian megalithic culture</li><li>Painted Grey Ware culture</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The Kacchi Plain of Balochistan, Pakistan, near the Bolan Pass, west of the Indus River, between Quetta,…</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The plains of the Indus and of the seasonal Ghaggar-Hakra river and their borderlands, in most of…</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The western Gangetic plain and the Ghaggar-Hakra valley, with the Sutlej and upper Ganga-Yamuna valleys…</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>South India, with key sites in Tamil Nadu and Karnataka, with related graffiti marks in Central India and…</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The northern Indian subcontinent</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Ban Chiang, Nong Han district, Udon Thani province, northeast Thailand</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p><b>Mehrgarh culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;Mehrgarh is one of the earliest known places in South Asia where people farmed barley and wheat and herded sheep, goats and cattle, living in mud-brick houses.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Indus Valley Civilisation</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;The most extensive of the first urban civilisations, it covered more ground than Egypt and Mesopotamia together, with over a thousand known sites and great cities such as Harappa and Mohenjo-daro.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Ban Chiang culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;Ban Chiang is a village site in northeast Thailand, found in 1966, whose graves run from a Neolithic farming community to the Iron Age.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose two of these cultures that lived at the same time. What did they have in common, and what set them apart?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=South%20%26%20Southeast%20Asia. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
